# Release signing config — TEMPLATE ONLY (committed, non-secret).
#
# Copy into the `app/` Gradle module dir as `keystore.properties` (gitignored) — i.e.
# mobile/android/app/keystore.properties — and fill in REAL values for a local signed
# release build. This template lives one level up (mobile/android/), so from here run:
#     cp keystore.properties.example app/keystore.properties   # from mobile/android/
#
# build.gradle reads `app/keystore.properties` (resolved relative to the android/ Gradle
# project). When the file is ABSENT, `assembleRelease` still succeeds and produces an
# UNSIGNED apk — it is NEVER downgraded to the debug key. Presence of this file IS the flag.
#
# CI (.github/workflows/build-apk.yml) writes this file from GitHub Actions secrets
# (KEYSTORE_BASE64 / KEYSTORE_PASSWORD / KEY_ALIAS / KEY_PASSWORD) and shreds it afterward.
#
# storeFile is resolved by file(...) relative to mobile/android/app/, so a bare filename
# lives at mobile/android/app/jaghelm-release.jks. See docs/mobile/KEYSTORE.md for the
# keytool command + GitHub secret setup.
#
# NOTE: values are intentionally UNQUOTED placeholders — never paste a real password here.
storeFile=jaghelm-release.jks
storePassword=CHANGE_ME
keyAlias=jaghelm-upload
keyPassword=CHANGE_ME
